WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.975
Who does what?

2
00:00:00.975 --> 00:00:04.562
Platform and pipeline engineers
own the scheduled checks.

3
00:00:04.562 --> 00:00:09.336
Identity engineers close findings, and
they close them at the source, the owner

4
00:00:09.336 --> 00:00:14.037
of the fact, because a fix made in the
directory just comes back on the next feed.

5
00:00:14.037 --> 00:00:17.762
The next run closes a finding
only if the source changed.

6
00:00:17.762 --> 00:00:20.058
And the I S S O receives the evidence,

7
00:00:20.058 --> 00:00:25.420
checks every package with nothing more than
a checksum tool, and signs the period.
